   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output A.1. Enhanced decent work statistics using innovative sources and statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Timor-Leste conducted Labour Force Survey in 2021 in line with the guidelines from the 20th International Conference of Labour Statisticians of October 2018. The 2021 Labour Force Survey is the third stand-alone full Labour Force Survey carried out in Timor-Leste since the country&#x2019;s independence in 2002. The first Labour Force Survey in Timor-Leste was conducted in 2010, the second was conducted in 2013.
The survey was conducted in September &#x2013; November 2021, finalised in 2022 and the LFS analytical report was launched on 26 January 2023.  The 2021 LFS was conducted by the General Directorate of Statistics (GDS), Ministry of Finance, in close collaboration with the Secretariat of State for Vocational Training and Employment (SEFOPE).
The 2021 Labour Force Survey provided updated data on the employment and labour market situation in the country, which will provide evidence to stimulate dialogue on economic development and employment, to see changes in the labour market situation and to provide a good platform to build future knowledge about the intricate relationship between the national economy, education, skills, and employment trends, and to use for planning and monitoring the social and economic progress, as well as for industrial relations. The 2021 LFS also include an insight on the current impact of the pandemic on the Timor-Leste labour market: impact on both (possible) job losses, as well as impact on employment conditions (working time, earnings, etc.) for those still in employment. The ILO provided assistance to the Government of Timor-Leste in conducting 2021 Labour Force Survey (LFS). The ILO working in close collaboration with the General Directorate of Statistics (GDS) under the auspices of the Ministry of Finance and Labour Market Information (LMI) Department within the Secretariat of State for Vocational Training and Employment (SEFOPE) in carrying out the survey, including designing questionnaires, data processing and tabulation, and producing the final analytical report of 2021 LFS.</narrative>
   </description>
